<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sonoma, California</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sonoma is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-francisco">San Francisco</a> Bay, that grew around the Mission San Francisco Solano, the last of the California missions, founded in 1823. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mariano-guadalupe-vallejo">Mariano Guadalupe Vallejo</a> laid out its plaza in 1835. In June 1846 the Bear Flag revolt began there with the seizure of the town, and it is now a centre of California's wine country.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sonoma-california.jpg" alt="Sonoma, California" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cullen328 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sonoma_City_Hall_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
